  "summary": "Oakland County, Michigan commissioners approved a nine-month Flock Safety drone pilot program for the sheriff's office, with an optional $2.5M two-year contract to follow. The article summarizes safeguards, public opposition over privacy and potential ICE access, law enforcement success stories, and contrasts with Ferndale, which ended its Flock partnership after finding outside agencies dominated queries with bizarre justifications.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Oakland County approved a nine-month pilot program to deploy seven Flock Safety drones, a decision that includes an optional transition into a $2.5 million, two-year contract.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "Ferndale Councilwoman Laura Mikulski revealed that her city's own police accounted for less than 1% of the queries into their license-plate reading system, while outside agencies from as far away as Texas accessed the data for reasons labeled in the log as \"thirsty\" or \"hamburger.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
